From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase, ntdll, server: application hives (RegLoadAppKey), performance key behaviour, RegQueryInfoKey

RegLoadAppKey returned the made-up handle 0xdeadbeef.  It now loads the
hive file (made when missing) as a private hive under \Registry\A without
privileges, writes it back when the root handle is closed or flushed and
unloads it; NtLoadKeyEx takes REG_APP_HIVE and returns the root handle
(INVALID_PARAMETER_7 for a root handle without it), and wow64 passes that
handle back.  The server lets \Registry\A hives be saved and unloaded
without the backup/restore privileges.  RegQueryInfoKey reports the key's
security descriptor size and leaves a zero-size class buffer's length at 0.
The performance keys behave as on Windows: opening them from themselves,
RegSetValueEx on the text keys (BADKEY), RegEnumKey (NO_MORE_ITEMS),
RegEnumValue (MORE_DATA), RegQueryInfoKey (two values), a too small data
buffer keeps its size, and the System object is the default object.
Their todo_wine marks are removed from the advapi32 and ntdll tests.

---
